# data/orders/trade_log.csv is an append-only log that multiple GitHub Actions workflows (and
# possibly a local push) can all try to commit new rows to around the same time. Standard git
# merge/rebase treats two commits that each add a new line at the same position (end of a short
# file) as a genuine conflict, not an auto-mergeable change -- confirmed by direct testing, not
# assumed. `merge=union` tells git to keep both sides' added lines instead of conflicting,
# exactly the behavior wanted for a shared append-only log. Requires each workflow to also run
# `git config merge.union.driver "git merge-file --union %A %O %B"` before rebasing/merging --
# see the "Persist trade log / risk state" step in .github/workflows/*.yml.
data/orders/trade_log.csv merge=union
